1
00:00:02,679 --> 00:00:06,750
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:08,051 --> 00:00:09,953
Hm.  I better reload.

3
00:00:09,953 --> 00:00:12,422
Never know when I'll be making
new friends around here.

4
00:00:14,424 --> 00:00:18,061
Huh, we've got so many dead bodies,
we're hanging them from the ceiling now.

5
00:00:19,262 --> 00:00:20,797
And the ceiling eats them.

6
00:00:20,797 --> 00:00:21,865
Guess that works.

7
00:00:22,499 --> 00:00:23,266
Wha-hoah!

8
00:00:23,266 --> 00:00:25,335
That shock just got the face-hugger!

9
00:00:25,335 --> 00:00:26,803
And another one!

10
00:00:26,803 --> 00:00:27,871
Will this guy make it?

11
00:00:28,538 --> 00:00:29,873
No!

12
00:00:29,873 --> 00:00:31,808
You're all popcorn.

13
00:00:31,808 --> 00:00:35,078
That really does have
to be more than coincidence.

14
00:00:35,078 --> 00:00:35,512
I mean--GYAH!

15
00:00:35,512 --> 00:00:36,713
[explosion]
I mean--GYAH!

16
00:00:36,713 --> 00:00:39,149
Okay, I guess I'm not going that way.

17
00:00:39,149 --> 00:00:40,384
Where am I going?

18
00:00:40,917 --> 00:00:42,986
The blood trail's
gone up into the ceiling.

19
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:46,223
Ah!
"Administrative offices..."

20
00:00:46,523 --> 00:00:47,824
Yeah, no exit!

21
00:00:47,824 --> 00:00:49,159
No one leaves here.

22
00:00:49,159 --> 00:00:50,060
What's that say?

23
00:00:51,094 --> 00:00:53,363
"Work harder, not smarter."

24
00:00:53,363 --> 00:00:54,831
Yeah, that's us, alright.

25
00:00:54,831 --> 00:00:57,300
We stay the course with stupid.

26
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:58,201
Hey, there's somebody in there.

27
00:00:58,201 --> 00:00:58,835
[scientist screaming]
Hey, there's somebody in there.

28
00:00:58,835 --> 00:01:01,171
Hey, quit screwing around
and open the door!

29
00:01:02,205 --> 00:01:02,906
Come on!

30
00:01:03,473 --> 00:01:05,208
The door's locked, assholes!

31
00:01:05,909 --> 00:01:06,910
Dammit!

32
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:10,781
Y'know, it's hard to believe we won
the Cold War with initiative like that.

33
00:01:10,781 --> 00:01:15,018
That's not the spirit that kept
Soviet paratroopers off my lawn.

34
00:01:15,018 --> 00:01:19,156
If somebody knocks on the door, you
don't run away and go play with aliens.

35
00:01:20,323 --> 00:01:21,925
Ah, an air vent.

36
00:01:21,925 --> 00:01:24,327
Die Hard has shown me the way once again.

37
00:01:25,862 --> 00:01:27,831
Now we're making progress.

38
00:01:28,331 --> 00:01:29,433
I think.

39
00:01:29,866 --> 00:01:30,200
What?

40
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:31,301
BUG!

41
00:01:32,969 --> 00:01:34,938
This is MY air vent.

42
00:01:35,872 --> 00:01:37,507
Hey, this is a dead end.

43
00:01:37,507 --> 00:01:39,009
And so are you!

44
00:01:41,411 --> 00:01:43,880
DIE DIE DIE DIE DIE!

45
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:46,049
These bugs think they own the place.

46
00:01:46,049 --> 00:01:48,819
Well, there's going to be some
restructuring around here.

47
00:01:48,819 --> 00:01:50,787
Oh, there's another one.

48
00:01:50,787 --> 00:01:52,889
That's right.
Keep running, you little bastard.

49
00:01:52,889 --> 00:01:55,125
I see you thinking
you're going to escape.

50
00:01:55,992 --> 00:01:57,427
Well, you're WRONG!

51
00:01:57,427 --> 00:01:59,362
Just like everyone else here!

52
00:01:59,362 --> 00:02:00,964
RRAAAAAH!

53
00:02:00,964 --> 00:02:04,634
Man, today is so counterintuitive
to everything I did in grad school.

54
00:02:04,634 --> 00:02:08,105
I would shout and break stuff there,
too, but that never got anything done.

55
00:02:08,638 --> 00:02:11,908
So, what's the deal
with--AAHHH...

56
00:02:11,908 --> 00:02:12,909
Grody!

57
00:02:12,909 --> 00:02:14,544
I hate this place.

58
00:02:14,544 --> 00:02:15,645
[pattering sound]
What's that noise?

59
00:02:16,012 --> 00:02:19,716
Ugh, that makes not even want to
loot the machine now.

60
00:02:19,716 --> 00:02:21,852
I was going to grab some Doritos
or something.

61
00:02:23,453 --> 00:02:26,123
Oh, but look who it is.

62
00:02:26,123 --> 00:02:27,991
[ceiling tiles fall]
What?

63
00:02:27,991 --> 00:02:28,792
Don't interrupt me.

64
00:02:29,659 --> 00:02:31,561
The man who can't open the door.

65
00:02:31,561 --> 00:02:32,195
SCIENTIST: Gordon...

66
00:02:32,195 --> 00:02:32,763
Yes?

67
00:02:32,763 --> 00:02:34,664
SCIENTIST: If I had known it was
you, I'd have let you in.

68
00:02:34,664 --> 00:02:35,465
Of course.

69
00:02:35,465 --> 00:02:36,733
SCIENTIST: Everyone's heading
for the surface.

70
00:02:37,134 --> 00:02:38,969
SCIENTIST: But I think they're
crazy not to stay put.

71
00:02:39,503 --> 00:02:41,505
SCIENTIST: Someone is bound to
come by and rescue us.

72
00:02:41,505 --> 00:02:42,839
Well, I believe you.

73
00:02:42,839 --> 00:02:45,008
But, does my gun believe you?

74
00:02:45,008 --> 00:02:46,409
Oh, all right.

75
00:02:46,409 --> 00:02:49,412
I'll let you live, but you're on
the preliminary list.

76
00:02:50,413 --> 00:02:51,581
What's this?

77
00:02:51,581 --> 00:02:52,582
"High voltage"?

78
00:02:52,582 --> 00:02:55,585
Cool.  Maybe I can fry those
things hanging from the ceiling.

79
00:02:56,119 --> 00:02:57,587
Oh, that turned it off.

80
00:02:57,954 --> 00:02:58,555
Oh well.

81
00:02:58,855 --> 00:03:01,658
I wonder if that guy's right
about--Don't puke on me.

82
00:03:01,658 --> 00:03:03,593
--that guy's right about waiting here.

83
00:03:03,593 --> 00:03:07,798
I would feel stupid if there was a
rescue team waiting in the lobby.

84
00:03:08,165 --> 00:03:10,333
All right, looks like that cut the power.

85
00:03:10,333 --> 00:03:15,272
Now, I can pass safely, proving once
again that I am superior to aliens.

86
00:03:15,806 --> 00:03:16,873
And everyone.

87
00:03:16,873 --> 00:03:19,242
[whistling]

88
00:03:19,242 --> 00:03:19,976
[lock jiggles]

89
00:03:19,976 --> 00:03:20,610
What?!

90
00:03:20,610 --> 00:03:23,180
I WENT THROUGH THAT
OBSTACLE COURSE FOR THIS?!

91
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:24,881
I HATE THIS BUILDING!

92
00:03:24,881 --> 00:03:26,817
I WANT TO SMASH THE WHOLE THING DOWN!

93
00:03:26,817 --> 00:03:27,884
[glass shatters]
I WANT TO SMASH THE WHOLE THING DOWN!

94
00:03:27,884 --> 00:03:29,719
Oh, well that works.

95
00:03:29,719 --> 00:03:31,822
Maybe I should
become a burglar after this.

96
00:03:31,822 --> 00:03:35,258
I'm getting the hang of breaking-
and-entering and I like stealing stuff.

97
00:03:35,258 --> 00:03:36,860
Wow, glad that's not my lab.

98
00:03:37,794 --> 00:03:39,830
"Scheduled Chaos Theory"?

99
00:03:39,830 --> 00:03:42,365
That makes as much sense as
"Grounded Aviation".

100
00:03:42,365 --> 00:03:44,067
Or "Deep Sea Astronomy".

101
00:03:44,067 --> 00:03:46,269
[locks jiggle]

102
00:03:46,269 --> 00:03:47,470
Of course.

103
00:03:47,470 --> 00:03:48,905
Every door is locked.

104
00:03:48,905 --> 00:03:50,173
Always.

105
00:03:50,173 --> 00:03:52,209
Why is every door locked?

106
00:03:52,209 --> 00:03:53,743
This is a workday.

107
00:03:53,743 --> 00:03:55,946
It's not like I'm breaking out
on Sunday evening.

108
00:03:56,646 --> 00:03:59,349
Ah!  Thought I didn't see you, huh?

109
00:03:59,349 --> 00:04:02,152
I'm watching.  I'm always watching.

110
00:04:04,087 --> 00:04:06,823
Well, the sign was right.
This looks like storage.

111
00:04:06,823 --> 00:04:08,225
Another dead end.

112
00:04:08,225 --> 00:04:11,027
This must be the prep room
for the crate-smashing room.

113
00:04:11,027 --> 00:04:13,663
Crate City: For All Your
Creative Crate Needs

114
00:04:13,663 --> 00:04:14,397
[growls]

115
00:04:14,397 --> 00:04:17,500
Y'know, I'm torn between wanting to
kill every single bug in this building

116
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:19,603
or just leveling it with explosives.

117
00:04:20,036 --> 00:04:20,937
I need a bomb.

118
00:04:22,105 --> 00:04:24,407
Nah, that's probably a janitor closet.

119
00:04:24,407 --> 00:04:26,877
This window kind of reminds me
of when I came home from school

120
00:04:26,877 --> 00:04:29,946
and there was some dead guy stuck
in the smashed window of my apartment.

121
00:04:29,946 --> 00:04:31,681
He had been trying to break into the place,

122
00:04:31,681 --> 00:04:34,517
but instead gutted himself on
the insulated glass.

123
00:04:34,517 --> 00:04:37,587
That was not fun trying to
explain that to the police.

124
00:04:38,255 --> 00:04:39,990
Oh, what's that?

125
00:04:39,990 --> 00:04:41,191
Another air vent.

126
00:04:41,691 --> 00:04:44,895
These people locking doors think
they're smart, but they're not.

127
00:04:44,895 --> 00:04:47,063
Guess I'd better clear out all
this glass, first.

128
00:04:47,530 --> 00:04:49,532
I'm kind of like glass, in a way.

129
00:04:49,532 --> 00:04:52,135
I'll tear people to shreds when
I can't do my job.

130
00:04:52,702 --> 00:04:56,706
All right, so, this is not
very comfortable.

131
00:04:56,706 --> 00:04:58,141
[screaming]

132
00:04:58,141 --> 00:05:01,611
Okay!  That water's got some
electricity running through it.

133
00:05:01,611 --> 00:05:04,748
I didn't really plan for that,
but, that's okay.

134
00:05:05,181 --> 00:05:05,982
That's okay.

135
00:05:06,383 --> 00:05:07,350
I can do this.

136
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:08,919
I just need a breather for a second.

137
00:05:09,419 --> 00:05:10,787
Yeah, I can do this.

138
00:05:10,787 --> 00:05:13,523
Hell, I've gotten hit with
Tasers that do more than that.

139
00:05:13,823 --> 00:05:16,459
Women are too damned jumpy with
those things.

140
00:05:16,459 --> 00:05:19,629
I swear, half the dates I go on,
it's just 'zap'.

141
00:05:19,629 --> 00:05:21,464
That's not as bad as pepper
spray, though.

142
00:05:21,464 --> 00:05:22,832
God, I hate pepper spray.

143
00:05:23,166 --> 00:05:25,669
[shuddering]

144
00:05:25,669 --> 00:05:27,737
[exhaling]

145
00:05:27,737 --> 00:05:29,506
Oh, you son of a bitch.

146
00:05:29,839 --> 00:05:31,107
[ringing]

147
00:05:31,107 --> 00:05:32,742
[ringing]
Gyeeeeaaaaaaggggghhhh...

148
00:05:32,742 --> 00:05:34,411
[ringing]
My ears!

149
00:05:34,411 --> 00:05:36,579
[ringing]
That was not smart.

150
00:05:36,579 --> 00:05:39,482
[ringing]
Firing a gun inside an air vent...

151
00:05:39,482 --> 00:05:41,284
[ringing]
I hope I'm not deaf...

152
00:05:41,284 --> 00:05:42,852
[ringing]
I need a silencer.

153
00:05:42,852 --> 00:05:43,386
[ringing]

154
00:05:43,386 --> 00:05:45,288
[ringing]
And that whole electrical shock thing

155
00:05:45,288 --> 00:05:47,123
[ringing]
reminds me of that guy I used to know.

156
00:05:47,123 --> 00:05:47,924
[ringing fades]
What was his name?

157
00:05:47,924 --> 00:05:49,659
Jessie.  He was crazy.

158
00:05:49,659 --> 00:05:50,627
He would--eugh.

159
00:05:51,494 --> 00:05:54,597
He would lie on his bed then
drop a cattle-prod on his leg

160
00:05:54,597 --> 00:05:59,336
with the voltage set so high he would
just be paralyzed there for an hour or two.

161
00:05:59,336 --> 00:06:01,104
He did that all the time for fun.

162
00:06:04,207 --> 00:06:07,310
Personally, I could think of better ways
to spend an evening--AH SHIT!

163
00:06:08,144 --> 00:06:11,614
Yep, whoever designed this
building did not count on me.

164
00:06:11,614 --> 00:06:12,515
[ceiling tiles fall]

165
00:06:12,515 --> 00:06:13,984
Oh, copy cats!

166
00:06:16,086 --> 00:06:18,054
Forgot to copy that move, huh?

167
00:06:18,521 --> 00:06:19,889
Actually, I'd better shut up.

168
00:06:19,889 --> 00:06:23,326
It would be just my luck for these
aliens to figure out how to use guns.

169
00:06:23,326 --> 00:06:24,694
Any more takers?

170
00:06:24,694 --> 00:06:25,261
No?

171
00:06:25,695 --> 00:06:26,529
All right, let's--

172
00:06:26,529 --> 00:06:27,597
[lock jiggles]

173
00:06:27,597 --> 00:06:28,698
--cry...

174
00:06:28,698 --> 00:06:31,634
This locked door thing is
getting real old.

175
00:06:31,634 --> 00:06:34,704
Ay yi yi yi yi yi...

176
00:06:34,704 --> 00:06:36,239
What now?

177
00:06:36,239 --> 00:06:38,742
Well, back to crawling in the
ceiling like a voyeur.

178
00:06:41,878 --> 00:06:44,614
[Steve Irwin accent]
Ah, the hunter spots his prey.

179
00:06:45,348 --> 00:06:46,750
He takes aim.

180
00:06:47,984 --> 00:06:48,451
[heacrab squeals]

181
00:06:48,451 --> 00:06:48,985
[heacrab squeals]
Crikey!

182
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:52,789
And that's about as close as it gets!

183
00:06:53,189 --> 00:06:55,859
[regular accent]
Now what are aliens doing up here, anyway?

184
00:06:57,193 --> 00:07:00,463
I guess they must've teleported in,
but how do they know where to go?

185
00:07:00,463 --> 00:07:01,898
Ohh, maybe they don't!

186
00:07:01,898 --> 00:07:03,933
Maybe they're teleporting into the walls.

187
00:07:03,933 --> 00:07:05,935
That could be why
the building's falling apart.

188
00:07:05,935 --> 00:07:08,304
We're turning into the
Swiss Cheese of the Damned.

189
00:07:11,408 --> 00:07:13,710
Wait, what if one teleported inside me?

190
00:07:14,511 --> 00:07:16,379
Oh, geez, I don't think
I could take that.

191
00:07:18,048 --> 00:07:19,649
[whistling noise]
Whoa, what happened here?

192
00:07:19,649 --> 00:07:22,118
[turret firing]
Agh! God!  Jeez!  Shit!

193
00:07:22,118 --> 00:07:23,053
[turret firing]
What was that?!

194
00:07:23,053 --> 00:07:24,587
[turret firing]
Who's firing?!

195
00:07:24,587 --> 00:07:25,755
[turret beeps]
Did I get hit?

196
00:07:25,755 --> 00:07:27,323
[turret beeps]
I don't see any blood.

197
00:07:27,323 --> 00:07:28,324
[turret beeps]
If I could just see--

198
00:07:28,324 --> 00:07:29,426
[turret firing]
FUCK!

199
00:07:29,426 --> 00:07:30,293
[turret beeps]
It's like...

200
00:07:30,293 --> 00:07:31,694
[turret beeps]
It's like a turret gun or something.

201
00:07:31,694 --> 00:07:32,395
[turret firing]

202
00:07:32,395 --> 00:07:33,129
[turret firing]
You okay?

203
00:07:33,129 --> 00:07:33,663
[turret beeps]

204
00:07:33,663 --> 00:07:34,864
[turret beeps]
Eh, I don't care.

205
00:07:34,864 --> 00:07:37,067
[turret beeps]
Jesus Christ!

206
00:07:37,067 --> 00:07:39,569
[turret beeps]
Oh, some clips, I'll take that.

207
00:07:39,569 --> 00:07:41,237
[turret beeps]
Yes!  An exit.

208
00:07:41,237 --> 00:07:42,138
[turret beeps]

209
00:07:42,138 --> 00:07:46,676
[turret beeps]
Oh my God! This is where I just came from!

210
00:07:46,676 --> 00:07:48,344
[turret beeps]
Maybe that's why all the doors are locked.

211
00:07:48,344 --> 00:07:51,614
[turret deactivates]
To keep people like me from
wandering into a firing range.

212
00:07:51,614 --> 00:07:53,083
Hey, want to be my human shield?

213
00:07:53,083 --> 00:07:53,783
SCIENTIST: Shut up!

214
00:07:53,783 --> 00:07:54,884
It was just an idea.

215
00:07:55,685 --> 00:07:59,155
Um... no, that's just a dead end.

216
00:07:59,155 --> 00:08:01,624
Maybe I could force him out
there if I waved my gun at him.

217
00:08:01,624 --> 00:08:02,525
SCIENTIST: Oh-ooooh...!

218
00:08:02,525 --> 00:08:04,160
Shit, did I say that out loud?

219
00:08:04,727 --> 00:08:05,795
[whistling noise]
Yep, it's still there.

220
00:08:05,795 --> 00:08:07,163
[turret firing]

221
00:08:07,163 --> 00:08:08,465
[turret beeps]
Okay.

222
00:08:08,465 --> 00:08:09,332
[turret beeps]

223
00:08:09,332 --> 00:08:10,467
[turret beeps]
Well, this is about as good a time

224
00:08:10,467 --> 00:08:11,601
[turret beeps]
to take a break as any.

225
00:08:11,601 --> 00:08:13,601
[turret beeps]

